  hero: {
    question: ['一百多种元素，为什么能排进一张表？表上的位置怎样决定一种元素会形成什么化合物、什么晶体、什么颜色？', 'How do a hundred-odd elements fit into one table, and how does a place in that table decide what compounds, crystals and colours an element forms?'],
    lead: ['无机化学研究除碳氢化合物以外的全部元素和它们的化合物：从氢、碱金属、卤素和稀有气体，到过渡金属、镧系锕系，再到固体、矿物和生物体里的金属。它的主线是周期律：原子的电子排布决定了半径、电离能和电负性，这些又决定了成键方式、酸碱性和氧化还原性。本馆八章从原子讲到晶体和元素化学，最后一章介绍正在改变这门学科的新方向。', 'Inorganic chemistry studies every element and its compounds apart from the hydrocarbons: hydrogen, the alkali metals, halogens and noble gases, the transition metals, lanthanides and actinides, and the solids, minerals and metals of living things. Its backbone is periodicity: electron configuration sets atomic radius, ionisation energy and electronegativity, and these in turn set bonding, acid–base and redox behaviour. Eight chapters go from atoms to crystals and the chemistry of the elements, ending with the directions now reshaping the field.'],
    scope: ['配合物的配体场、电子光谱、磁性和金属有机催化放在 [[chemistry/coordination/index.html|07 配位与金属有机化学]]；晶体学、点群和衍射放在 [[chemistry/structural/index.html|05 结构化学]]；功能材料和多孔框架放在 [[chemistry/materials/index.html|11 材料化学]]；原子轨道本身的量子力学在 [[quantum/physics/index.html|量子物理展馆]]。这里讲的是这些内容在“元素和它们的化合物”层面上的样子。', 'Ligand fields, electronic spectra, magnetism and organometallic catalysis are in [[chemistry/coordination/index.html|07 Coordination & Organometallic]]; crystallography, point groups and diffraction in [[chemistry/structural/index.html|05 Structural]]; functional materials and porous frameworks in [[chemistry/materials/index.html|11 Materials]]; the quantum mechanics of atomic orbitals in the [[quantum/physics/index.html|Quantum Physics pavilion]]. This hall treats them at the level of the elements and their compounds.'],
  },
